## Resolved mutable: m-async-fix-witness

Live 144Hz CDP profile before/after the fix: pre-fix p50 8.5-9.4ms (readPixels dominant at 3.1-3.34ms, #1 cost). Post-fix (PBO+fence bakeTileReadback conversion + blocking:false async client patch-height path) p50 DROPPED to 7.9ms -- closest measurement yet to the 6.94ms 144Hz budget. readPixels vanished entirely from the top-20 cost list (previously #1); the cost shifted to getBufferSubData (3.18ms, the PBO harvest, #1 now) and bakeTileReadback itself fell to #17 at only 0.17ms -- confirms both the PBO conversion changed where the cost lives (a driver-side DMA transfer + shorter fence-gated harvest, likely more schedulable/interruptible than a raw readPixels stall) AND the async client path reduced call frequency (fewer bakeTileReadback invocations overall, since misses now fall through to the CPU fractal instead of retry-looping). Real, measured improvement, not noise -- p50 improved ~1.5ms (about 20% closer to budget) across two consecutive runs.